[[File:Chelsea 4 Spurs 2 (34175049426).jpg|thumb|alt=Chelsea players celebrating|Chelsea players celebrating a goal in the semi-final match against Tottenham Hotspur]]
[[Chelsea F.C.|Chelsea]] also started their FA Cup campaign in the third round where they were drawn at home at [[Stamford Bridge (stadium)|Stamford Bridge]] against [[EFL League One|League One]] side [[Peterborough United F.C.|Peterborough United]].  The home side took the lead through [[Pedro (footballer, born 1987)|Pedro]], and [[Michy Batshuayi]] doubled their advantage before half-time.  [[Willian (footballer, born 1988)|Willian]] made it {{nowrap|3&ndash;0}} seven minutes after the interval before [[John Terry]] was [[Penalty card#Red card|sent off]] for a foul on [[Lee Angol]].  Three minutes later, [[Tom Nichols (footballer)|Tom Nichols]] scored for Peterborough but Pedro scored with 15 minutes to go to make the final score {{nowrap|4&ndash;1}}.<ref>{{cite web |last=Reddy |first=Luke |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/38481659 |title=Chelsea 4–1 Peterborough United |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=8 January 2017 |access-date=22 April 2017 |archive-date=6 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075150/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/38481659 |url-status=live }}</ref> In the fourth round, they were drawn against Championship team [[Brentford F.C.|Brentford]] at home.   Goals from Willian and Pedro made it {{nowrap|2&ndash;0}} after 21 minutes, before [[Branislav Ivanović]]'s goal on the [[Glossary of association football terms#B|break]] and a [[penalty kick (association football)|penalty]] from Batshuayi gave Chelsea a {{nowrap|4&ndash;0}} victory.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/38700669 |title=Chelsea 4–0 Brentford |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=28 January 2017 |access-date=22 April 2017 |archive-date=6 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075238/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/38700669 |url-status=live }}</ref> 

In the fifth round, Chelsea faced Championship side [[Wolverhampton Wanderers F.C.|Wolverhampton Wanderers]] away at [[Molineux Stadium|Molineux]].  After a goalless first half, Pedro gave Chelsea the lead with a [[Header (association football)|header]] midway through the second before [[Diego Costa]] secured a {{nowrap|2&ndash;0}} win with a low strike in the 89th minute.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/38940092 |title=Wolverhampton Wanderers 0–2 Chelsea |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=18 February 2017 |access-date=22 April 2017 |archive-date=6 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075304/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/38940092 |url-status=live }}</ref>  In the quarter-final, Chelsea were drawn at home against fellow Premier League side and [[2016 FA Cup final|FA Cup holders]] [[Manchester United F.C.|Manchester United]].  [[Ander Herrera]] was sent off for Manchester United in the 35th minute for a second [[Penalty card#Yellow card|yellow card]] before [[N'Golo Kanté]] scored the game's solitary goal early in the second half with a low driven shot which beat [[David de Gea]].<ref>{{cite web |last=McNulty |first=Phil | authorlink = Phil McNulty| url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/39176050 |title=Chelsea 1–0 Manchester United |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=13 March 2017 |access-date=22 April 2017 |archive-date=6 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075246/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/39176050 |url-status=live }}</ref> In the semi-final at Wembley Stadium, Chelsea took on  [[Tottenham Hotspur F.C.|Tottenham Hotspur]], their [[Chelsea F.C.–Tottenham Hotspur F.C. rivalry|London rivals]].  Willian gave Chelsea the lead in the fifth minute with a [[Free kick (association football)|free kick]] before [[Harry Kane]] equalised with a low header.  [[Son Heung-min]] was adjudged to have fouled on [[Victor Moses]] on 43 minutes and Willian converted the subsequent penalty to give Chelsea a {{nowrap|2&ndash;1}} half-time lead.  [[Dele Alli]] equalised from a [[Christian Eriksen]] pass early in the second half but strikes from [[Eden Hazard]] and [[Nemanja Matić]] secured a {{nowrap|4&ndash;2}} win for Chelsea and qualification for the final.<ref>{{cite web |last=McNulty |first=Phil | authorlink = Phil McNulty| url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/39604653 |title=Chelsea 4–2 Tottenham Hotspur |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=22 April 2017 |access-date=22 April 2017 |archive-date=6 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075256/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/39604653 |url-status=live }}</ref>

==Pre-match==
Arsenal were appearing in the FA Cup final for the 20th time, and for the third time in four years. They had won the cup twelve times, and were beaten finalists seven times; most recently in [[2001 FA Cup final|2001]].{{efn|Arsenal had won the FA Cup in [[1930 FA Cup final|1930]], [[1936 FA Cup final|1936]], [[1950 FA Cup final|1950]], [[1971 FA Cup final|1971]], [[1979 FA Cup final|1979]], [[1993 FA Cup final|1993]], [[1998 FA Cup final|1998]], [[2002 FA Cup final|2002]], [[2003 FA Cup final|2003]], [[2005 FA Cup final|2005]], [[2014 FA Cup final|2014]] and [[2015 FA Cup final|2015]].<ref name=facupfinals>{{Cite web | url = https://www.thefa.com/competitions/thefacup/stories/fa-cup-finals | publisher = [[The Football Association]] | access-date = 10 April 2021 | title = FA Cup Finals the winners' list}}</ref>}}  By comparison, Chelsea were making their 12th appearance in a FA Cup final.<ref>{{cite web |title=Arsenal vs Chelsea, match preview |url=http://www.skysports.com/football/arsenal-vs-chelsea/preview/371643 |publisher=[[Sky Sports]] |date=26 May 2017 |access-date=26 June 2017 |archive-date=6 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075246/https://www.skysports.com/football/arsenal-vs-chelsea/preview/371643 |url-status=live }}</ref> The club won the cup seven times and lost four finals.{{efn|Chelsea had won the FA Cup in [[1970 FA Cup final|1970]], [[1997 FA Cup final|1997]], [[2000 FA Cup final|2000]], [[2007 FA Cup final|2007]], [[2009 FA Cup final|2009]], [[2010 FA Cup final|2010]] and [[2012 FA Cup final|2012]].<ref name=facupfinals/>}} The clubs had previously met 13 times in the FA Cup. Arsenal held an advantage in those meetings, winning seven of the last eight; Chelsea won the last FA Cup tie, a {{nowrap|2–1}} victory in April 2009.<ref name=bbc>{{cite web |title=Arsenal v Chelsea |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/39984089 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170527113654/http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/39984089 |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=27 May 2017 |archive-date=27 May 2017 |access-date=26 June 2017}}</ref> This was the second FA Cup final to feature both sides; the first was won by Arsenal in 2002.<ref>{{cite web |title=Arsenal vs Chelsea 2002 FA Cup finalists – where are they now? |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/football/2017/05/26/arsenal-vs-chelsea-2002-fa-cup-finalists-now/ |work=[[The Daily Telegraph]] |date=26 May 2017 |access-date=26 June 2017 |archive-date=6 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075233/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/football/2017/05/26/arsenal-vs-chelsea-2002-fa-cup-finalists-now/ |url-status=live }}</ref>
[[File:Conte UDI-ATA 1-3.jpg|thumb|upright|alt=Antonio Conte|Chelsea manager [[Antonio Conte]] was on course to win the [[Double (association football)#England|domestic double]] in his first season at the club.]]
The most recent meeting between the two teams was a league encounter in February 2017, Chelsea winning by three goals to one, a result which moved them 12 points clear in first position.<ref>{{cite web |title=Eden Hazard mesmerises Arsenal to tighten Chelsea's Premier League grip |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2017/feb/04/chelsea-arsenal-premier-league-match-report |newspaper=[[The Observer]] |date=5 February 2017 |access-date=26 June 2017 |archive-date=6 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075318/https://www.theguardian.com/football/2017/feb/04/chelsea-arsenal-premier-league-match-report |url-status=live }}</ref> The victory was significant given that Chelsea had lost the reverse fixture 3–0 in September 2016, in what BBC journalist [[Phil McNulty]] described as a "watershed moment" in their season.<ref>{{cite web |first=Phil |last=McNulty | authorlink=Phil McNulty|title=Chelsea 3–1 Arsenal |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/38779302 |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=4 February 2017 |access-date=26 June 2017 |archive-date=6 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075237/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/38779302 |url-status=live }}</ref> While Arsenal struggled to build momentum throughout autumn and winter, Chelsea manager [[Antonio Conte]]'s tactical switch from [[Formation (association football)#4.E2.80.933.E2.80.933|4–3–3]] to [[Formation (association football)#3.E2.80.934.E2.80.933|3–4–3]] thereafter resulted in a 13-match winning run.<ref>{{cite web |first=Phil |last=McNulty | authorlink=Phil McNulty |title=Arsenal: Are Arsene Wenger's side spurning title chance again? |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/38359736 |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=18 December 2016 |access-date=26 June 2017 |archive-date=6 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075318/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/38359736 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name="champs">{{cite web |first=Phil |last=McNulty | authorlink=Phil McNulty| title=Chelsea are Premier League champions: How did Antonio Conte do it? |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/39885837 |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=12 May 2017 |access-date=26 June 2017 |archive-date=6 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075237/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/39885837 |url-status=live }}</ref> They won the Premier League with two matches to spare,<ref name="champs"/> and later set a new divisional record for the most wins (30).<ref>{{cite web |title=Are Chelsea champions of the year-on-year football points swing? |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2017/may/31/are-chelsea-champions-of-the-year-on-year-football-points-swing |work=[[The Guardian]] |date=31 May 2017 |access-date=26 June 2017 |archive-date=6 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075234/https://www.theguardian.com/football/2017/may/31/are-chelsea-champions-of-the-year-on-year-football-points-swing |url-status=live }}</ref> 
Arsenal ended the season in fifth place, their lowest placing under manager [[Arsène Wenger]], missing out on [[UEFA Champions League]] football for the first time in 20 years.<ref>{{cite web |first1=JJ |last1=Bull |first2=Jeremy |last2=Wilson |title=How Liverpool secured Champions League spot as Arsenal fell short |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/football/2017/05/21/premier-league-final-day-live-score-updates-arsenal-liverpool/ |work=[[The Daily Telegraph]] |date=21 May 2017 |access-date=26 June 2017 |archive-date=6 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075227/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/football/2017/05/21/premier-league-final-day-live-score-updates-arsenal-liverpool/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Wenger's future had been cast into doubt following a bad run of form in February and March, which included the team losing {{nowrap|10–2}} on aggregate against [[FC Bayern Munich|Bayern Munich]] in the Champions League, the worst [[aggregate score|aggregate]] performance by an English club in the history of the tournament.<ref>{{Cite web | url = https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/39152642 | publisher = [[BBC Sport]] | title = Arsenal 1&ndash;5 Bayern Munich | first = Saj | last = Chowdhury | access-date = 10 April 2021 | date = 7 March 2017}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web | url = https://www.11v11.com/teams/arsenal/tab/matches/season/2017/ | website = 11v11 | publisher = AFS Enterprises | access-date = 10 April 2021 | title = Arsenal football club match record: 2017}}</ref>

To arrest the decline, Wenger adopted a similar tactical change to Conte, playing three defenders at the back.<ref>{{cite web |title=FA Cup final manager focus: Antonio Conte v Arsene Wenger |url=http://sport.bt.com/football/fa-cup-final-manager-focus-antonio-conte-v-arsene-wenger-S11364182481963 |publisher=[[BT Sport]] |date=23 May 2017 |access-date=26 June 2017 |archive-date=6 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075332/http://sport.bt.com/football/fa-cup-final-manager-focus-antonio-conte-v-arsene-wenger-S11364182481963 |url-status=live }}</ref> Arsenal went on to win eight of their last nine fixtures, but Wenger suggested his team were not favourites: "it's quite even or maybe Chelsea are ahead, so it's a bit similar to what happened in the semi-final against Manchester City. That's part of what makes it all exciting as well."<ref>{{cite web |title=Wenger – Breaking record not my priority |url=http://www.arsenal.com/news/news-archive/20170524/wenger-breaking-record-not-my-priority |publisher=[[Arsenal F.C.]] |date=24 May 2017 |access-date=26 June 2017 |archive-date=6 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075332/https://www.arsenal.com/news/news-archive/20170524/wenger-breaking-record-not-my-priority |url-status=live }}</ref> Of his future he said, "It will not be my last match anyway, because I will stay, no matter what happens, in football."<ref>{{cite web |first=James |last=Olley |title=FA Cup Final will not determine Arsene Wenger's future |url=https://www.standard.co.uk/sport/football/arsenal-vs-chelsea-fa-cup-final-will-not-determine-arsene-wenger-future-a3547461.html |newspaper=[[Evening Standard|London Evening Standard]] |date=24 May 2017 |access-date=27 June 2017 |archive-date=6 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075332/https://www.standard.co.uk/sport/football/arsenal-vs-chelsea-fa-cup-final-will-not-determine-arsene-wenger-future-a3547461.html |url-status=live }}</ref> Former Arsenal player [[Paul Merson]]'s evaluation was, "Mertesacker is going to be crucial for Arsenal if he plays; he will have to play very well if Arsenal are to have any chance. If he doesn't play well then Chelsea are going to cut through Arsenal like a knife through butter."<ref>{{cite web |title=Paul Merson's FA Cup final prediction: Chelsea set for comfortable win over Arsenal |url=http://www.skysports.com/football/news/11095/10891760/paul-mersons-fa-cup-final-prediction-chelsea-set-for-comfortable-win-over-arsenal |first=Paul |last=Merson | authorlink = Paul Merson | publisher=[[Sky Sports]] |date=27 May 2017 |access-date=27 June 2017 |archive-date=6 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075336/https://www.skysports.com/football/news/11095/10891760/paul-mersons-fa-cup-final-prediction-chelsea-set-for-comfortable-win-over-arsenal |url-status=live }}</ref>

Conte described Wenger as one of the "greats" in football, and felt he would remain as Arsenal manager come the season's end.<ref name="preview">{{cite web |title=FA Cup final: Arsene Wenger one of the game's greats – Antonio Conte |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/40062358 |publisher=[[BBC Sport]] |date=4 February 2017 |access-date=27 June 2017 |archive-date=6 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075342/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/40062358 |url-status=live }}</ref> "He has done a fantastic job. Sometimes in England I think you undervalue the achievement of qualifying for the Champions League. Only this season they haven't qualified for the Champions League," he continued.<ref name="preview"/> Conte reiterated the importance of his players keeping their focus and wanted Chelsea to "pay great attention and focus" to their opponents.<ref>{{cite web |first=Ben |last=Burrows |title=Chelsea boss Antonio Conte doesn't think FA Cup final will be Arsene Wenger's last game in charge of Arsenal |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/fa-league-cups/antonio-conte-press-conference-arsenal-vs-chelsea-fa-cup-final-preview-a7757896.html |newspaper=[[The Independent]] |date=26 May 2017 |access-date=27 June 2017 |archive-date=6 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075249/https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/fa-league-cups/antonio-conte-press-conference-arsenal-vs-chelsea-fa-cup-final-preview-a7757896.html |url-status=live }}</ref> Hazard, who was playing in his first FA Cup final, was eager to win the competition: "For Chelsea, for such a big club like this, you need to win one, two, three trophies every season if you can. Now we have the possibility to win another trophy so all the players are ready for that. It's such a great competition for the fans."<ref name="preview"/>

[[File:Arsenal 2 Chelsea 1 (35008804615).jpg|thumb|alt=Banners and stadium before the game|Banners and stadium before the game]]
While Chelsea had no injury or suspension worries, Arsenal had doubts over the fitness of [[Petr Čech]] and [[Shkodran Mustafi]], and were already without defenders [[Laurent Koscielny]] (suspension) and Gabriel (ankle injury).<ref name="squad">{{cite web |first=David |last=Hytner |title=Arsenal v Chelsea: match preview |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2017/may/26/arsenal-chelsea-match-preview |newspaper=[[The Guardian]] |date=26 May 2017 |access-date=27 June 2017 |archive-date=6 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075245/https://www.theguardian.com/football/2017/may/26/arsenal-chelsea-match-preview |url-status=live }}</ref> [[Per Mertesacker]] was expected to start; the [[Germany national football team|Germany international]] only featured once for Arsenal's first team during the season.<ref>{{cite web |first=Jeremy |last=Wilson |title=Arsenal captain Per Mertesacker could be forced to start FA Cup final |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/football/2017/05/24/arsenal-captain-per-mertesacker-could-forced-start-fa-cup-final/ |newspaper=[[The Daily Telegraph]] |date=24 May 2017 |access-date=26 June 2017 |archive-date=6 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075227/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/football/2017/05/24/arsenal-captain-per-mertesacker-could-forced-start-fa-cup-final/ |url-status=live }}</ref>  The day before the final ''[[The Guardian]]'' reported that Wenger chose [[David Ospina]] to start in goal ahead of Čech.<ref>{{cite web |first=David |last=Hytner |title=Arsène Wenger drops Petr Cech and gives David Ospina nod for FA Cup final |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2017/may/26/petr-cech-injury-hands-david-ospina-fa-cup-final-start-for-arsenal |newspaper=[[The Guardian]] |date=26 May 2017 |access-date=26 June 2017 |archive-date=6 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075248/https://www.theguardian.com/football/2017/may/26/petr-cech-injury-hands-david-ospina-fa-cup-final-start-for-arsenal |url-status=live }}</ref> 

Both clubs received an allocation of approximately 28,000 tickets.<ref name="tick">{{cite web |title=2017 Emirates FA Cup Final details confirmed |url=http://www.thefa.com/news/2017/apr/25/the-emirates-fa-cup-final-details-250417 |publisher=[[The Football Association]] |date=25 May 2017 |access-date=27 June 2017 |archive-date=13 October 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191013160454/http://www.thefa.com/news/2017/apr/25/the-emirates-fa-cup-final-details-250417 |url-status=live }}</ref> For adults, these were priced £45, £65, £85 and £115, with concessions in place.<ref name="tick"/> Chelsea supporters were situated in the west side of the ground, while Arsenal's were allocated in the east.<ref>{{cite web |first=Luke |last=Brown |title=Arsenal and Chelsea supporters allocated 28,000 tickets for next month's FA Cup final at Wembley |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/fa-league-cups/fa-cup-final-details-released-arsenal-chelsea-fans-tickets-a7701766.html |newspaper=[[The Independent]] |date=25 April 2017 |access-date=26 June 2017 |archive-date=6 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075251/https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/fa-league-cups/fa-cup-final-details-released-arsenal-chelsea-fans-tickets-a7701766.html |url-status=live }}</ref>  The remaining 14,000 tickets were distributed to what the FA described as the "football family which includes volunteers representing counties, leagues, local clubs and charities".<ref name="tick"/> The losing finalist would receive £1.6{{nbsp}}million in total prize money while the winners earned a total of £3.4{{nbsp}}million.<ref>{{cite web |first=Joe |last=Hall |title=FA Cup prize money 2017: How much prize money will Arsenal or Chelsea receive for winning the trophy? |url=http://www.cityam.com/256555/fa-cup-third-round-much-winning-worth-its-prize-money |newspaper=[[City A.M.]] |date=27 May 2017 |access-date=27 June 2017 |archive-date=6 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075303/https://www.cityam.com/fa-cup-third-round-much-winning-worth-its-prize-money/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Security at Wembley Stadium was tightened in the wake of the [[Manchester Arena bombing]] and Arsenal cancelled a screening of the game at their ground.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/fa-league-cups/arsenal-cancel-fa-cup-final-screening-vs-chelsea-manchester-terror-attack-security-threat-a7753326.html |title=Arsenal cancel FA Cup final screening at Emirates Stadium due to security threat after Manchester terror attack |last=De Menezes |first=Jack |date=25 May 2017 |access-date=27 June 2017 |work=[[The Independent]] |archive-date=6 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075254/https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/fa-league-cups/arsenal-cancel-fa-cup-final-screening-vs-chelsea-manchester-terror-attack-security-threat-a7753326.html |url-status=live }}</ref> Both clubs cancelled plans for [[open top bus]] victory parades.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/football/2017/05/24/chelsea-cancel-premier-league-victory-parade-light-manchester/|title=Chelsea cancel Premier League victory parade in light of Manchester terror attack|date=24 May 2017|work=[[The Daily Telegraph]]|access-date=26 May 2017|archive-date=6 January 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075255/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/football/2017/05/24/chelsea-cancel-premier-league-victory-parade-light-manchester/|url-status=live}}</ref> 

The game was broadcast live in the United Kingdom by both [[BBC]] and [[BT Sport]]. [[BBC One]] provided the free-to-air coverage and BT Sport 2 was the pay-TV alternative.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/latestnews/2017/fa-cup-final|title=FA Cup Final 2017 across the BBC|date=25 May 2017|publisher=[[BBC News]]|access-date=26 May 2017|archive-date=6 January 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075144/https://www.bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/latestnews/2017/fa-cup-final|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=http://sport.bt.com/football/arsenal-v-chelsea-live-stream-the-fa-cup-final-online-or-watch-on-tv-with-bt-sport-S11364182537399|title=Arsenal v Chelsea: Live stream the FA Cup final online or watch on TV with BT Sport|date=23 May 2017|publisher=[[BT Sport]]|access-date=26 May 2017|archive-date=6 January 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075228/http://sport.bt.com/football/arsenal-v-chelsea-live-stream-the-fa-cup-final-online-or-watch-on-tv-with-bt-sport-S11364182537399|url-status=live}}</ref><!--  In North America, this was the first FA Cup Final to be televised by [[CTV Television Network|CTV]] in Canada and by [[Fox Broadcasting Company|FOX]] in the United States.{{cn|date=January 2021}}-->  It was the first time in the history of the FA Cup that a [[spidercam]] was utilised during the match.<ref>{{Cite web | url = https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/live/football/38395757?page=14 | publisher = [[BBC Sport]] | access-date = 7 January 2021 | title = Arsenal defeat Chelsea to win FA Cup (14 of 15) | first1 = Caroline | last1 = Chapman | first2 = Amy | last2 = Lofthouse | date = 27 May 2017 | archive-date = 21 March 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210321092555/https://www.bbc.com/sport/live/football/38395757/page/14 | url-status = live }}</ref>

[[Sol Campbell]] and [[Eddie Newton]] came onto the pitch to greet the supporters and place the trophy on a plinth.<ref name="daswf">{{cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/live/2017/may/27/arsenal-v-chelsea-2017-fa-cup-final-live|title=Arsenal 2–1 Chelsea: 2017 FA Cup final – as it happened|work = [[The Guardian]]|date=27 May 2017|access-date=30 June 2017|archive-date=14 June 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180614163938/https://www.theguardian.com/football/live/2017/may/27/arsenal-v-chelsea-2017-fa-cup-final-live|url-status=live}}</ref> As they departed, the traditional Cup Final hymn, "[[Abide with Me]]" was sung by representatives of eight clubs, including Lincoln City, [[Guernsey F.C.|Guernsey]], [[Millwall F.C.|Millwall]] and Sutton United.<ref name="prefi">{{cite web |title=2017 Emirates FA Cup Final details confirmed |url=http://www.thefa.com/news/2017/may/19/emirates-fa-cup-final-pre-match-entertainment-190517 |publisher=[[The Football Association]] |date=19 May 2017 |access-date=30 June 2017 |archive-date=6 January 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075305/https://www.thefa.com/news/2017/may/19/emirates-fa-cup-final-pre-match-entertainment-190517 |url-status=live }}</ref> The teams emerged moments later led by their managers, and players were greeted by [[Prince William, Duke of Cambridge]]. Soprano Emily Haig sang the national anthem and a minute's silence was then held to honour the victims of the Manchester attack.<ref name="daswf"/><ref name="prefi"/> Prince William, [[Mayor of Greater Manchester|Manchester Mayor]] [[Andy Burnham]], [[Secretary of State for Digital, Culture, Media and Sport|Culture Secretary]] [[Karen Bradley]] and FA chairman [[Greg Clarke]] laid wreaths on the pitch in tribute.<ref name="daswf"/>

==Match==
===Summary===
====First half====
[[File:Alexis Sanchez Arsenal Vs Burnley (24736448805) (cropped) (cropped).jpg|right|thumb|upright|alt=Alexis Sanchez|Alexis Sánchez ''(pictured in 2016)'' scored Arsenal's opening goal.]]
Arsenal [[Kick-off (association football)|kicked off]] the match around 5:30{{nbsp}}p.m. on 27 May 2017 at Wembley Stadium in front of 89,472 spectators. Chelsea lined up as a [[Formation (association football)#3–4–3|3–4–3 formation]] with Pedro, Costa and Hazard in attack, while Arsenal adopted a 3–4–2–1 with Welbeck up front.<ref name=bbc/> Arsenal dominated the early stages of the match and opened the scoring with a goal from Sánchez in the fourth minute, shooting past the advancing goalkeeper from {{convert|6|yd}} out with his right foot. The goal was initially flagged as [[Offside (association football)|offside]] as Ramsey was adjudged as being in an offside position.  After discussion with his assistant referee, the overrode the decision and awarded Arsenal the goal due to Ramsey not attempting to play the ball.  In the tenth minute, Ramsey was shown the first yellow card of the match.  In the 15th minute, Sánchez struck from distance but his shot was high, before Costa's shot from around {{convert|14|yd}} was blocked by Arsenal's defence.  A minute later, [[Mesut Özil]]'s side-footed shot was cleared off the line by [[Gary Cahill]].<ref name=bbcasit8>{{Cite web | title = Arsenal defeat Chelsea to win FA Cup (page 8)| first1 = Caroline | last1 = Chapman | first2 = Amy | last2= Lofthouse| publisher = [[BBC Sport]] | date = 27 May 2017 | access-date = 11 March 2021| url = https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/live/football/38395757?page=8}}</ref>  On 19 minutes, Arsenal hit the frame of Chelsea's goal twice in quick succession: Welbeck's header struck the post and the ball rebounded on Ramsey's chest from where it hit the post once more before going out.<ref name=bbcasit7/>

Midway through the half, Hazard passed to Moses whose shot was blocked before Mertesacker stopped Costa's shot.  On 29 minutes, a quick break from Arsenal ended with Welbeck opting to shoot from a narrow angle and Cahill making another goal-line clearance. Three minutes later, Sánchez's floated free kick fell to [[Granit Xhaka]] whose strike from distance was saved by [[Thibaut Courtois]], the Chelsea goalkeeper.<ref name=bbcasit7>{{Cite web | title = Arsenal defeat Chelsea to win FA Cup (page 7) | first1 = Caroline | last1 = Chapman | first2 = Amy | last2 = Lofthouse | publisher = [[BBC Sport]] | date = 27 May 2017 | access-date = 11 March 2021 | url = https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/live/football/38395757?page=7 | archive-date = 21 March 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210321092551/https://www.bbc.com/sport/live/football/38395757/page/7 | url-status = live }}</ref>  With six minutes of the half remaining, Pedro's shot from the edge of the Arsenal penalty area went over the crossbar.  Early in stoppage time, Monreal fouled Pedro near the box but Alonso's free kick was off-target and the half ended {{nowrap|1&ndash;0}}.<ref name=bbcasit6>{{Cite web | title = Arsenal defeat Chelsea to win FA Cup (page 6) | first1 = Caroline | last1 = Chapman | first2 = Amy | last2 = Lofthouse | publisher = [[BBC Sport]] | date = 27 May 2017 | access-date = 11 March 2021 | url = https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/live/football/38395757?page=6 | archive-date = 21 March 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210321092614/https://www.bbc.com/sport/live/football/38395757/page/6 | url-status = live }}</ref>

====Second half====
[[File:Arsenal 2 Chelsea 1 (34621140880).jpg|thumb|alt=Victor Moses being shown the red card|Moses receiving a red card in the second half]]
Neither side made any changes to their personnel during the interval and the second half kicked off with neither side dominating.  Four minutes in, Pedro's shot was blocked by Mertesacker before Kanté's powerful shot was caught by Ospina in the Arsenal goal.  Costa's attempt was then blocked by Mertesacker before Moses was kept out by Arsenal's defence.  In the 54th minute, [[Rob Holding]] was booked for bringing Costa down on the edge of the Arsenal penalty area: Pedro's subsequent free kick was headed clear by Mertesacker.<ref name=bbcasit5>{{Cite web | title = Arsenal defeat Chelsea to win FA Cup (page 5) | first1 = Caroline | last1 = Chapman | first2 = Amy | last2 = Lofthouse | publisher = [[BBC Sport]] | date = 27 May 2017 | access-date = 11 March 2021 | url = https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/live/football/38395757?page=5 | archive-date = 21 March 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210321092555/https://www.bbc.com/sport/live/football/38395757/page/5 | url-status = live }}</ref>  Two minutes later Moses was shown the yellow card for a foul on Welbeck before Kanté was booked for illegally blocking Ramsey.  In the 61st minute, Chelsea made the first substitution of the match when Matić was replaced by former Arsenal midfielder [[Cesc Fàbregas]].  [[Héctor Bellerín]] then took possession of the ball on the edge of the Chelsea penalty area after a run down the left wing by Welbeck, but his low shot was saved by Courtois diving to his left.  On 68 minutes, Moses fell in the Arsenal area while close to Monreal and appealed for a penalty but instead was shown his second yellow card by the referee for [[Diving (association football)|diving]] and was [[Ejection (sports)|sent off]]. With 18 minutes of the game remaining, Chelsea made their second change with Willian coming on for Pedro.<ref name=bbcasit4>{{Cite web | title = Arsenal defeat Chelsea to win FA Cup (page 4) | first1 = Caroline | last1 = Chapman | first2 = Amy | last2 = Lofthouse | publisher = [[BBC Sport]] | date = 27 May 2017 | access-date = 11 March 2021 | url = https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/live/football/38395757?page=4 | archive-date = 21 March 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210321092556/https://www.bbc.com/sport/live/football/38395757/page/4 | url-status = live }}</ref>
  
In the 76th minute, Costa scored for Chelsea to level the score at {{nowrap|1&ndash;1}}: he received the ball from Willian, chested it down and struck the ball past Ospina.  Giroud then came on for Welbeck, and 38 seconds later Arsenal re-took the lead: Ramsey headed the ball past Courtois after a cross from Giroud to make it {{nowrap|2&ndash;1}}.  With ten minutes remaining, [[David Luiz]] headed Willian's free kick into the side netting.  Arsenal's Oxlade-Chamberlain was then replaced by [[Francis Coquelin]] who was booked within a minute for a foul.  On 85 minutes, Bellerín received the ball on the halfway line and ran at Luiz, beating him before shooting wide of the Chelsea goal.  Costa's strike then hit Ospina squarely in the chest from close range.  Batshuayi came on in the 88th minute to replace Costa before Özil side-footed shot struck the Chelsea goal-post.<ref name=bbcasit3>{{Cite web | title = Arsenal defeat Chelsea to win FA Cup (page 3) | first1 = Caroline | last1 = Chapman | first2 = Amy | last2 = Lofthouse | publisher = [[BBC Sport]] | date = 27 May 2017 | access-date = 11 March 2021 | url = https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/live/football/38395757?page=3 | archive-date = 21 March 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210321092555/https://www.bbc.com/sport/live/football/38395757/page/3 | url-status = live }}</ref>  Three minutes into injury time, Arsenal brought on [[Mohamed Elneny]] to replace Sánchez.  After one further minute of stoppage time, the whistle was blown and Arsenal won the FA Cup final {{nowrap|2&ndash;1}}.<ref name=bbcasit2>{{Cite web | title = Arsenal defeat Chelsea to win FA Cup (page 2) | first1 = Caroline | last1 = Chapman | first2 = Amy | last2 = Lofthouse | publisher = [[BBC Sport]] | date = 27 May 2017 | access-date = 11 March 2021 | url = https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/live/football/38395757?page=2 | archive-date = 21 March 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210321092555/https://www.bbc.com/sport/live/football/38395757/page/2 | url-status = live }}</ref>

