==Post-match==
Winning the game secured a record 13th title for Arsenal, while Wenger became the most successful manager in the tournament's history with seven wins.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/fa-league-cups/arsenal-vs-chelsea-fa-cup-final-arsene-wenger-mikel-arteta-a9647501.html|title=How Arsene Wenger has helped Mikel Arteta prepare for FA Cup final|date=31 July 2020|work=[[The Independent]]|access-date=23 January 2021|archive-date=21 March 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210321092612/https://www.independent.co.uk/sport/football/fa-league-cups/arsenal-vs-chelsea-fa-cup-final-arsene-wenger-mikel-arteta-a9647501.html|url-status=live}}</ref>  Although winning the FA Cup would have secured a [[2017–18 UEFA Europa League]] group stage qualification, Arsenal had already qualified for the competition with a fifth-placed finish in the [[2016–17 Premier League]], which saw them fail to qualify for the [[2017–18 UEFA Champions League]].<ref>{{Cite news | url = https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/39912025 | title = Arsenal 3&ndash;1 Everton | access-date = 11 March 2021 | publisher = [[BBC Sport]] | first = Phil | last = McNulty | date = 19 May 2017 | authorlink = Phil McNulty | archive-date = 21 March 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210321092600/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/39912025 | url-status = live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web | url = https://www.premierleague.com/news/402785 | publisher = [[Premier League]] | access-date = 10 April 2021 | date = 25 May 2017 | title = Which clubs qualify for Europe in 2017/18?}}</ref> Due to the circumstances surrounding Mertesacker's appearance,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/football/2017/05/24/arsenal-captain-per-mertesacker-could-forced-start-fa-cup-final/|title=Arsenal captain Per Mertesacker could be forced to start FA Cup final|first=Jeremy|last=Wilson|date=24 May 2017|work=[[The Daily Telegraph]]|access-date=5 April 2018|archive-date=6 January 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075227/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/football/2017/05/24/arsenal-captain-per-mertesacker-could-forced-start-fa-cup-final/|url-status=live}}</ref> and performance on the day,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.mirror.co.uk/sport/football/news/fa-cup-final-2017-player-10513459|title=FA Cup Final player ratings as Sanchez steals the show at Wembley|first=John|last=Cross|date=27 May 2017|work=[[Daily Mirror]]|access-date=5 April 2018|archive-date=6 January 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075145/https://www.mirror.co.uk/sport/football/news/fa-cup-final-2017-player-10513459|url-status=live}}</ref> some Arsenal fans and former players have dubbed the game ''The Mertesacker Final''.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.arsenal.com/news/its-special-because-its-my-final-season#hpof2GXE7dtECMLo.99|title='It's special because it's my final season'|publisher=[[Arsenal F.C.]]|access-date=19 September 2017|archive-date=6 January 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210106075228/https://www.arsenal.com/news/its-special-because-its-my-final-season#hpof2GXE7dtECMLo.99|url-status=live}}</ref>

Welbeck praised his team but refused to be drawn on Wenger's future, saying "It was a great team performance{{nbsp}}... The manager is his own man and he makes his own decision and the board will make the right decision so I can't comment on that."<ref name=bbcasit2/>   Wenger himself focused on his team's display: "We had an outstanding performance from the first minute onwards. This team has suffered. They've united and responded."<ref name=bbcasit2/>  Chelsea goalkeeper Courtois refused to blame Moses for the defeat: "We are obviously disappointed but I want to say congratulations to Arsenal. They played a good game{{nbsp}}... we went down to 10 men and the red card was correct. Victor Moses doesn't need to apologise."<ref name=bbcasit>{{Cite web | title = Arsenal defeat Chelsea to win FA Cup (page 1) | first1 = Caroline | last1 = Chapman | first2 = Amy | last2 = Lofthouse | publisher = [[BBC Sport]] | date = 27 May 2017 | access-date = 11 March 2021 | url = https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/live/football/38395757 | archive-date = 21 March 2021 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20210321092621/https://www.bbc.com/sport/live/football/38395757 | url-status = live }}</ref>  Losing manager Conte said he had been surprised by Arsenal and that his side had started poorly: "Arsenal started very well with great determination. They surprised us a bit but I repeat our first 25 minutes weren't good{{nbsp}}... Our season was incredible to win the league in this way, it was great but now its important to look forward and to restart."<ref name=bbcasit/>

